  "hand_derivation": "The worked example of docs/fixtures/expected-math.md: quadratic, control points (0,0) (1,2) (3,2.5) (4,0), weights 1, 0.5, 2, 1, knots 0 (x3), 0.5, 1 (x3). Homogeneous points (w x, w y, w): P0w=(0,0,1), P1w=(0.5,1,0.5), P2w=(6,5,2), P3w=(4,0,1). On [0,0.5] the Bezier points are B0=P0w, B1=P1w, B2=(P1w+P2w)/2=(3.25,3,1.25). At the knot u=0.5 the point is B2, so (3.25/1.25, 3/1.25) = (2.6, 2.4). At u=0.25 it is (B0 + 2B1 + B2)/4 = (1.0625, 1.25, 0.8125), i.e. (17/13, 20/13). With all weights 1 the knot point would be (2, 2.25), so a renormalised weight-1 form is distinguishable.",
